      <div type="clause" n="92.4">
        <head><ref type="lawCode" target="law:Hn">Hn</ref> 92.4</head>
        <ab type="liebermannText" xml:lang="la" source="#liebermann" n="Hn 92.4" corresp="#wit-lat"><pb n="607" ed="#liebermann"/>Si sciatur, quis murdrum fecerit, et<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="43" target="#Hn_92-4.lnote.oe.43"/> fugerit, habeat hundretum<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="44" target="#Hn_92-4.lnote.oe.44"/> peccuniam eius; et si quis consociorum eius capiatur<ptr type="liebermannNote" n="45" target="#Hn_92-4.lnote.oe.45"/>, iusticie presentetur.</ab>
        <note type="editorial">New row (October 2026): Liebermann’s text transcribed from Gesetze I p. 607 (two independent readings of the page images, differences settled against the page)</note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_92-4.lnote.oe.43" n="43" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">607</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">fecerit <hi rend="italic">wiederholt, unterpunctirt Sc</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">fecerit repeated, dotted underneath for deletion Sc</seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_92-4.lnote.oe.44" n="44" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">607</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-edus <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-edus <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_92-4.lnote.oe.45" n="45" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">1</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">607</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de">-ietur <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude">-ietur <hi rend="italic">Lond</hi></seg></note>
        <note type="liebermannNote" subtype="textual" xml:id="Hn_92-4.lnote.oe._" n="-" source="#liebermann"><bibl><biblScope unit="volume">3</biblScope><biblScope unit="page">329</biblScope></bibl><seg type="original" xml:lang="de"><hi rend="italic">Ebd</hi>. Hundred 21b—92, 5 Am Rande spät: <hi rend="italic">In ista parte distinguit euidenter, quot modis et quibus iudicandum est murdrum</hi>—<hi rend="italic">in. esset</hi>{2}—<hi rend="italic">siatur</hi>{3} Rs</seg><seg type="translation" xml:lang="en" source="#claude"><hi rend="italic">Ibid</hi>. Hundred 21b—92, 5 in the margin, in a late hand: <hi rend="italic">In ista parte distinguit euidenter, quot modis et quibus iudicandum est murdrum</hi>—<hi rend="italic">in. esset</hi>{2}—<hi rend="italic">siatur</hi>{3} Rs</seg></note>
